# real_distinction: the distinction Mill affirms is one within utility (justice as a weightier kind of expediency), not the independent opposition S1–S2 may evoke.
# But A1 and C state the same "real, not imaginary" claim in the same terms, so I read no shift.
# justice_more_sacred: "sacred" in S2 (mankind's view) and S5 ("most sacred and binding") both mean having stronger binding force, so one sense.
